---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Section from '../components/Section.astro';
import StreamTimeline from '../components/StreamTimeline.astro';
import Gantt from '../components/Gantt.astro';
import VModel from '../components/VModel.astro';
import Figure from '../components/Figure.astro';
import { STREAMS, LESSONS } from '../data/timeline';
import { PLANNED, CTRL_ACTUAL, HW_ACTUAL, COMBINED, COMBINED_LINKS } from '../data/gantt';
import { fig } from '../lib/assets';
import { repoUrl, reportUrl } from '../lib/site';
---
<Base title="Story" description="How the Boost Brigade power shuffler came to be: the plan, the two streams of work, where they converged, and what the process taught.">
  <Section eyebrow="The story" title="Two streams that converged on one board" lede="A report tells you what was built. This page tells you how it went: the plan from the proposal, what each stream actually did, where the two met, and the lessons. Blue is the control stream, green is the hardware stream, amber is both." narrow />

  <Section alt eyebrow="The plan versus the reality" title="Three timelines" lede="The proposal planned three board revisions and an MPPT stage over 34 weeks. What happened instead was one board, one revision, and a lot of convergence in October. Switch between the views.">
    <div class="tabs" id="gantt-tabs" role="tablist">
      <button type="button" class="chip chip-accent" role="tab" aria-selected="true" data-tab="combined">Both streams, as it happened</button>
      <button type="button" class="chip" role="tab" aria-selected="false" data-tab="planned">The plan (proposal, 17 Apr)</button>
      <button type="button" class="chip" role="tab" aria-selected="false" data-tab="ctrl">Control stream, as it happened</button>
      <button type="button" class="chip" role="tab" aria-selected="false" data-tab="hw">Hardware stream, as it happened</button>
    </div>
    <div data-tab="combined"><Gantt tasks={COMBINED} links={COMBINED_LINKS} title="Both streams on one axis, with the hand-over points" /></div>
    <div data-tab="planned" hidden><Gantt tasks={PLANNED} title="The proposal's team Gantt: 34 weeks, V1 to V3 boards plus an MPPT" /><p class="small muted" style="margin-top:.6rem">From the project proposal, appendix B. Planned bars are dashed. <a class="ext" href={reportUrl('proposal')} target="_blank" rel="noopener">Proposal (PDF)</a></p></div>
    <div data-tab="ctrl" hidden><Gantt tasks={CTRL_ACTUAL} title="Control stream: teaching weeks with the milestone week of each phase" /><p class="small muted" style="margin-top:.6rem">From the delivery report, appendix A. <a class="ext" href={reportUrl('control', 33)} target="_blank" rel="noopener">Delivery report, p. 26</a></p></div>
    <div data-tab="hw" hidden><Gantt tasks={HW_ACTUAL} title="Hardware stream: planned versus actual milestones" />{fig('hw/gantt') && <Figure src={fig('hw/gantt')!} alt="Gantt chart of the planned and actual hardware schedule" caption="The hardware report's own Gantt: planned (grey) against actual (orange). The first schematic slipped into the mid-year break because of the inductor change and the late controller interface; the buffer weeks absorbed it." evidence={{ label: 'Hardware report, appendix 1', href: reportUrl('hardware', 29) }} width={1100} />}</div>
    <div class="callout" style="margin-top:1.5rem"><strong>What changed from the plan.</strong> The three-revision ladder (V1, V2 pair, V3 string) collapsed into a single Version 0 board that carried the whole feature set from day one, which cost the planned revision cycles. The MPPT stage was dropped from scope: the electronic load performs the string MPPT in every test. And the topology took longer to settle than planned, which held the control model until late in semester 1.</div>
  </Section>

  <Section eyebrow="How the work was run" title="The V-model, for both streams" lede="Each level produced a pass/fail artefact the next level consumed, so a fault could be isolated at the level where it was introduced. The control stream followed it explicitly; the hardware stream's simulation-first approach maps onto the same shape.">
    <VModel />
  </Section>

  <Section alt eyebrow="Divergence and convergence" title="The journey, side by side" lede="Control on the left, hardware on the right. The rails meet where the streams integrated: first at the hand-over of the QSPICE schematic and sensor set, then for good on reflow day.">
    <StreamTimeline entries={STREAMS} />
  </Section>

  <Section eyebrow="Lessons" title="What the process taught" lede="Reflective, not a complaints list: each of these changed how the next step was done.">
    <div class="grid grid-2">
      {LESSONS.map((l) => (
        <blockquote class:list={['lesson', l.stream]}><span class:list={['chip', l.stream === 'ctrl' ? 'chip-ctrl' : l.stream === 'hw' ? 'chip-hw' : 'chip-accent']}>{l.stream === 'ctrl' ? 'control' : l.stream === 'hw' ? 'hardware' : 'both'}</span><strong>{l.title}</strong> <span class="body">{l.body}</span></blockquote>
      ))}
    </div>
    <p class="small muted">Control lessons from <a class="ext" href={repoUrl('3_Analytical/shuffler_notebooks/DESIGN_LOG.md')} target="_blank" rel="noopener">DESIGN_LOG.md</a>, part 2; hardware lessons from the hardware report, §4.8 and §5.</p>
  </Section>
</Base>
<script>
  const tabs = document.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>('#gantt-tabs [data-tab]');
  tabs.forEach((b) => b.addEventListener('click', () => {
    tabs.forEach((x) => { x.setAttribute('aria-selected', 'false'); x.classList.remove('chip-accent'); });
    b.setAttribute('aria-selected', 'true'); b.classList.add('chip-accent');
    document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('#gantt-tabs ~ [data-tab]').forEach((d) => (d.hidden = d.dataset.tab !== b.dataset.tab));
  }));
</script>
<style>
  .tabs { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: .4rem; margin-bottom: 1rem; }
  .lesson { margin: 0; display: grid; gap: .4rem; font-size: 1rem; font-family: var(--font-body); background: var(--surface); border: 1px solid var(--line); border-left: 4px solid var(--accent); border-radius: 12px; padding: 1rem 1.1rem; }
  .lesson.ctrl { border-left-color: var(--blue); }
  .lesson.hw { border-left-color: var(--green); }
  .lesson strong { font-family: var(--font-display); font-size: 1.1rem; }
  .lesson .body { color: var(--muted); }
  .lesson .chip { justify-self: start; }
</style>
